 ### [DP-based Configuration Selector](15955-dp-based-configuration-selector.md)
 A method for selecting optimal NeRF configurations (geometry and texture parameters) for multiple segmented objects under a strict memory constraint $H$. It formulates the problem as a Multiple-Choice Knapsack (MCK) problem and uses dynamic programming to guarantee an optimal solution. It is chosen for mobile deployment where memory limits are critical.
 
+### [ActiveNeRF Training Configuration](16179-activenerf-training-configuration.md)
+A learning framework that models 3D scene uncertainty and uses an active learning scheme to select new training samples based on information gain. It supplements the existing training set with newly captured samples to improve model performance under limited training budgets. It is chosen when training data is scarce and active sampling can maximize information gain.
+
+### [Meta-learning for Fast NeRF Reconstruction](18591-meta-learning-for-fast-nerf-reconstruction.md)
+Enables rapid NeRF reconstruction from a small number of input images by leveraging gradient-based meta-learning. It learns an initialization or adaptation strategy that allows the scene representation MLP to converge in significantly fewer steps than standard training. It is chosen when fast adaptation to new scenes is required.
+
+### [Multi-scale and Mip-aware Representations](18780-multi-scale-and-mip-aware-representations.md)
+Encompasses training configurations that explicitly address aliasing and multi-scale reconstruction artifacts through specialized input encodings, activation functions, or supersampling strategies. It distinguishes itself by modifying the optimization loop to handle frequency content and resolution mismatches. It is chosen when rendering high-frequency details or avoiding aliasing artifacts.
+
+### [NARF Training](18818-narf-training.md)
+Optimizes a neural network to represent the radiance field of articulated 3D objects by minimizing photometric and mask errors. It distinguishes itself by incorporating known kinematic pose configurations into the rendering pipeline, allowing the model to disentangle geometry from articulation. It is chosen for training articulated objects where pose information is known.
+
 ### Blender Dataset Simplified Configuration
-A simplified training setup for the Blender dataset, designed for speed rather than maximum accuracy. It uses one round of sampling, 128 samples for the proposal MLP, and 32 samples for the NeRF MLP. The proposal MLP has 4 layers and 256 hidden units, while the NeRF MLP has 8 layers and 256 (or 512) hidden units. It uses axis-aligned Integrated Positional Encoding (IPE), MSE loss, and disables the distortion regularizer [S1].
